The constructions of (anti-)symmetric and compactly supported framelets ${\boldsymbol \Psi}$ are usually based on a multiresolution analysis (MRA); we first find some compactly supported refinable function $\phi$ with a refinement mask $q_0$ such that
\begin{align}\label{MRA-RF}
\phi=2^d\sum_{{\boldsymbol k}\in{\mathbb Z}^d}q_0[{\boldsymbol k}]\phi(2\cdot-{\boldsymbol k}).
\end{align}

\begin{align}\label{MRA-RF}
\phi=2^d\sum_{{\boldsymbol k}\in{\mathbb Z}^d}q_0[{\boldsymbol k}]\phi(2\cdot-{\boldsymbol k}).
\end{align}

Then the MRA based construction of ${\boldsymbol \Psi}=\left\{\psi_1,\cdots,\psi_r\right\}\subseteq L_2({\mathbb R}^d)$ is to find finitely supported masks $q_{\alpha}$ such that
\begin{align}\label{MRA-Fra}
\psi_{\alpha}=2^d\sum_{{\boldsymbol k}\in{\mathbb Z}^d}q_{\alpha}[{\boldsymbol k}]\phi(2\cdot-{\boldsymbol k}),~~~~~\alpha=1,\cdots,r.
\end{align}

\begin{align}\label{MRA-Fra}
\psi_{\alpha}=2^d\sum_{{\boldsymbol k}\in{\mathbb Z}^d}q_{\alpha}[{\boldsymbol k}]\phi(2\cdot-{\boldsymbol k}),~~~~~\alpha=1,\cdots,r.
\end{align}

Briefly speaking, as long as $\left\{q_0,q_1,\cdots,q_r\right\}$ are compactly supported and their Fourier series $\widehat{q}_{\alpha}({\boldsymbol{\xi}})=\sum_{{\boldsymbol k}\in{\mathbb Z}^d}q_{\alpha}[{\boldsymbol k}]e^{-i{\boldsymbol{\xi}}\cdot{\boldsymbol k}}$ satisfy
\begin{align}\label{UEP}
\sum_{\alpha=0}^r\left|\widehat{q}_{\alpha}({\boldsymbol{\xi}})\right|^2=1~~~~\text{and}~~~~\sum_{\alpha=0}^r\widehat{q}_{\alpha}({\boldsymbol{\xi}})\overline{\widehat{q}_{\alpha}({\boldsymbol{\xi}}+\boldsymbol{\nu})}=0
\end{align}
for all $\boldsymbol{\nu}\in\left\{0,\pi\right\}^d\setminus\left\{\0\right\}$ and ${\boldsymbol{\xi}}\in[-\pi,\pi]^d$, the quasi-affine system ${\mathscr X}({\boldsymbol \Psi})$ with ${\boldsymbol \Psi}=\left\{\psi_1,\cdots,\psi_r\right\}$ defined by \cref{MRA-Fra} forms a tight frame of $L_2({\mathbb R}^d)$, and the filters $\left\{q_0,q_1,\cdots,q_r\right\}$ form a discrete tight frame on $\ell_2({\mathbb Z}^d)$ \cite{B.Dong2013}.

\begin{align}\label{UEP}
\sum_{\alpha=0}^r\left|\widehat{q}_{\alpha}({\boldsymbol{\xi}})\right|^2=1~~~~\text{and}~~~~\sum_{\alpha=0}^r\widehat{q}_{\alpha}({\boldsymbol{\xi}})\overline{\widehat{q}_{\alpha}({\boldsymbol{\xi}}+\boldsymbol{\nu})}=0
\end{align}

